<h1><span data-field="title" data-format="default">weak_ref_alive</span></h1>
<p>With this function you can check the <a class="tooltip" title="A weak reference is a reference that does not protect the referenced object from collection by a garbage collector, and so can be used to check if a struct is still &quot;alive&quot; (referenced) or not somewhere in the game.">weak reference</a> to a struct to see if it is still &quot;alive&quot; or not. You supply the weak reference to check (as returned by the function <span class="inline3_func"><a href="weak_ref_create.htm">weak_ref_create</a></span>), and the function will return <span class="inline2">true</span> if the struct is still being referenced somewhere or <span class="inline2">false</span> if it&#39;s not and has been garbage collected. Note that if you supply a value that is not a weak reference, the function will return <span class="inline2">undefined</span>.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-field="title" data-format="default">weak_ref_alive</span>(weak_ref)</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>weak_ref</td>
<td><span data-keyref="Type_Struct_WeakRef"><a target="_blank" href="weak_ref_create.htm">Struct Weak Reference</a></span></td>
<td>The weak reference to the struct you want to check.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Bool"><a target="_blank" href="../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Boolean</a></span> (or undefined)</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">if (weak_ref_alive(inventory_ref))<br/>
{<br/>
    inventory = -1;<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above code checks a weak reference to a struct and if it is still alive the variable referencing it is set to -1, de-referencing the struct and enabling it to be garbage collected.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
